  {
   "id": 3,
   "ref": "96–98",
   "en": "And it [hasn't escaped|1,4] me that you've been afraid all along, [suspicious of|9,10] our walls, of the homes of high Carthage. But where will it end? What is the point now of such a contest?'",
   "en_marked": "[And|1] it [hasn't escaped|1,4] [me|2] that [you've|6] [been afraid|5] {all along|Not in the Latin. Added to bring out the perfect tense of habuisse: Venus has been suspicious for some time.}, [suspicious of|9,10] [our|8] [walls|7], of the [homes|11] of [high|13] [Carthage|12]. [But|14] [where|15] [will|16] it [end|17]? [What|19] {is the point|Added to make the English work: quo (to what end) needs a verb, and the Latin leaves it out.} [now|20] of [such|22] a [contest|21]?'",
